{"ver": "0.1", "info": {"id": "wdd3R7", "date": "1568133554", "viewed": 305, "name": "rotating oriental pattern 1", "username": "FabriceNeyret2", "description": "based on 4-branches cross contra-rotative along a checker grid.", "likes": 5, "published": 3, "flags": 0, "usePreview": 0, "tags": ["pattern", "tiling", "cross", "2tweets", "gif", "short", "golf", "islamic", "reproduction"], "hasliked": 0, "parentid": "", "parentname": ""}, "renderpass": [{"inputs": [], "outputs": [{"id": "4dfGRr", "channel": 0}], "code": "// Fork of  https://shadertoy.com/view/wd3GR7\n// NB: -2 by moving A= inside S macro at first use, but would be really ugly ;-)\n// funny: ceil(U) instead of floor create artifacts at some resolutions\n   \n\n\nvoid mainImage(out vec4 O, vec2 u) {\n    vec2 R = iResolution.xy,\n         U = 3.* (u+u-R)/R.y, A = mod(floor(U),2.);\n    A = abs( 3.1*(fract(U)-.5) * mat2(cos(vec4(0,33,11,0) +(A.x==A.y?1.:-1.)*iTime))),\n    O += .5 - ( min(A.y,A.x) -.5 ) /30. *R.y;\n//  O += sin(12.* clamp( .5 - ( min(A,A.x) -.5 ) /420. *R , 0., 1. ).y) // variant\n}", "name": "Image", "description": "", "type": "image"}]}